-- title:
--   Igusa-chart place lies over a supersingular place (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ is a valuation subring with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the set of nonunits of $A$; $k :=$ `ResidueField A` is its residue field.
--
--   The two function fields in play are $\mathcal F :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and $\mathcal G :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the level-$\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ function field, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Over the residue field one has `modularFunctionFieldC k M'`, the $k$-subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k M'`, and `xHFunctionFieldC k (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, generated over $k$ by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$. `Place K F` is the structure consisting of a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $\top$ and a principal ideal ring; `ord`, `evalAt` and `IsRational` are its order function, its residue evaluation and the surjectivity of $K \to$ (residue field of the place).
--
--   The data and hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` over $k$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' k`, that is of those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace k M'` and whose value $w$.`evalAt (jGeomGen k M')` lies in `ssJSet q k`.
--
--   *Fields and constant reduction.* `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathcal F \le \mathcal G$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathcal F$ along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC k M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\mathcal F$ whose constants are exactly those of $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants, such that every nonzero element of $\mathcal F$ can be rescaled by a constant into `R₀.integers` with nonzero residue, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of elements of nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires in addition that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose pushforward to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in $\mathcal F$, that pushforward lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a $k$-Laurent series, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *A uniformiser in $A$.* $\pi \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (hypothesis `hπ`) and $\pi \in A$ (hypothesis `hπP`). Further $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   *The two families of valuation subrings of $\mathcal G$.* $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal G$ to each point $\ell$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ ([`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21)), and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ assigns one to each $s \in W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which characterises $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$ at $\ell_\infty =$ `lineInfty q` $= [1 : 0]$ as the set of $f \in \mathcal G$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ to $k$ is nonzero and $f \cdot (y$ pushed to $\bar{\mathbb Q})= (x$ pushed to $\bar{\mathbb Q})$; `hIg`, which provides for each $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ` $\cdot \ell_\infty = \ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ equal to the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which for all $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ gives a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma \ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, saying that for every $s$ and every $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ the constant $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, saying that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is (that is, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for every place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\hat\jmath)$, where $\hat\jmath$ denotes the element of $\mathcal F$ given by the coefficientwise image of `jq`) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal G$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $k$ equals $s$.`evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and the constant $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, the invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, which provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   *Descent data.* $K_0$ is a subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi \in K_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (hypothesis `hιK₀`), such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (hypothesis `hres`); $\varpi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (hypothesis `hϖ₀`) and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ (hypothesis `hϖ₀π`). $F_0$ is a subfield of $\mathcal G$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; `hjF₀` asserts that the image of $\hat\jmath$ in $\mathcal G$ lies in $F_0$, and this element of $F_0$ is assumed nonzero. Finally $F_0$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map is, by `hj₀`, given on each $a \in A_0$ by the constant $\iota(a)$ of $\mathcal G$.
--
--   *The reading data.* Fix $s \in W$ and $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and write $O_\ell$ for the valuation subring `(OIg ℓ).comap F₀.subtype` of $F_0$. The homomorphism $\rho$ goes from the residue field of $O_\ell$ to `xHFunctionFieldC k (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, and $\tau$ is a ring endomorphism of the $k$-Laurent series which, by `hτ`, is either the identity or `qExpand k (q ^ 2)`. The compatibilities required of $\rho$ are: `hρA`, that for $a \in A_0$ whose image in $F_0$ lies in $O_\ell$, $\rho$ of the residue class of that image is the constant $\iota(a)$ reduced to $k$; and `hρf`, that for $f \in$ `R₀.integers`, $a \in A_0$ and $g$ in `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ F₀ ĵ` — the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\hat\jmath$ — with $g \in O_\ell$ and $g$ equal in $\mathcal G$ to the image of $f$ minus the constant $\iota(a)$, the Laurent expansion of $\rho$ of the residue class of $g$ equals $\tau$ of the expansion of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ minus the constant given by the residue of $\iota(a)$ in $k$.
--
--   Finally $w$ is a place of `xHFunctionFieldC k (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $k$, subject to two conditions: `hwC`, that $\rho$ of the residue class of every $g$ in `chartAlgFin A₀ F₀ ĵ` lying in $O_\ell$ belongs to the valuation subring of $w$; and `hread`, that whenever $f \in$ `R₀.integers` is regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is (in the sense of the order condition above) and its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then for every $a \in A_0$ whose image $\iota(a)$ has residue in $k$ equal to $s$.`evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, and every $g$ in `chartAlgFin A₀ F₀ ĵ` lying in $O_\ell$ and equal in $\mathcal G$ to the image of $f$ minus the constant $\iota(a)$, the element $\rho$ of the residue class of $g$ lies in the nonunits of the valuation subring of $w$.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses, for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` and every $g' \in$ `xHFunctionFieldC k (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` whose Laurent expansions satisfy $g' = \tau(g)$, the element $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $g'$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$.
--
--   This is the step asserting that a place $w$ of the reduced level-$\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ function field which reads the Igusa chart at $\ell$ correctly — containing the images under $\rho$ of all chart residues, and sending to nonunits the residues of the normalised differences $f - a$ at a supersingular place $s$ — lies over $s$ along the $\tau$-twisted inclusion of the level-$M'$ field, in the case $q = 2$. It is used in the identification of places of the semistable covering, where it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_valuationSubring_residueField_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_descent_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_valuationSubring_residueField_igusaRing_of_floorTrace_descent_of_eq_two).
